--[[
The Ward: the town of the lower city, under the seawall. Houses of two and three stories, the Registry and its dome on
the market square, the clock tower, the canal with its old bridge and its basin, the Water Gate to the harbor in the
east, the Foundry gate in the south. Every door the player can reach opens (see the interiors in `links`).

The wall of the city: the Registry, Tally, the Water Gate and the Foundry gate are for citizens. The player gets their
tide-mark as Coral (see npcs.luau): her mother's letter in the Ebb house says her token is in her boat, in the basin of
the old bridge, out of reach from the banks. The ferry of the wetlands sails the canal.

Lenses (see lenses.luau): a yellow one on the square, in front of the Registry, one at the Water Gate, one at the
Foundry gate; crimson ones (they always see) over the old bridge and on the south street. A lens that sees the player
starts a lockdown. Ways around: time the sweeps, sail the canal, or crawl through the duct under it (the west vents).
]]
